  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273146/assets/3a75e2c0b7606508eca7ae172ee79a2510022bdb8575de122b7ac7c43c55fb96.png)\n\nThe Venn diagram shown above represents two events $X$ and $Y$ and the probabilities of each event. Calculate $P(Y|X).$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute $P(Y|X),$ we need to ask, \"what is the probability of $Y$ occurring given that $X$ has occurred?\"\n\nSince we are assuming that $X$ has occurred, we only consider the events inside $X.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273146/assets/96e36af7abc98925b1c70aa832913dc19ac46ec988dea71e4c6efba6a39966ed.png)\n\nThe probability of event $X$ occurring is\n\n$$\nP(X)=0.42+0.18=0.6.\n$$\n\nNow, $P(Y|X)$ can be interpreted as the proportion of $Y$ that lies inside $X,$ relative to the size of $X.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y|X)=\\frac{0.18}{0.6}=0.3.\n$$",
